// RemClaw Debug Environment
// Note: $() is an xcconfig trick to produce a literal "//"
// Use scripts/update-local-ip.sh to rewrite host to your current LAN IP.

// ─── Backend API URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Debug points at STAGING so dev builds exercise current code before it reaches prod, and
// staging has its own database, so nothing built from here can touch real user data.
//
// ⚠️ THIS BLOCK ALREADY SAID EXACTLY THAT WHILE POINTING AT A LAPTOP. On 2026-08-11 the active
// line was `http://192.168.1.x:3000` — a LAN address that resolves on one machine, on one
// network — and these comments still claimed staging. A build from it reached no backend at all,
// and the symptom was "Apple sign-in couldn't finish", which sends you looking at iCloud instead
// of at the URL. The wrong comment cost far more than the wrong value.
//
// ⚠️ DO NOT EDIT THIS LINE TO POINT SOMEWHERE ELSE. Use the untracked local override at the
// bottom of this file instead (`RemClaw/Debug.local.xcconfig`) — that is what it is for, it
// cannot be committed by accident, and it leaves this file honest for everyone else.
API_BASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR_BACKEND_URL
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID = YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID = com.googleusercontent.apps.YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
IAP_PRO_PRODUCT_ID = YOUR_IAP_PRO_PRODUCT_ID

// PostHog Telemetry Configuration
POSTHOG_API_KEY = YOUR_POSTHOG_API_KEY
POSTHOG_HOST = https:/$()/us.i.posthog.com

// ─── Optional local overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Untracked (see .gitignore) and absent by default, so a fresh clone builds with the values
// above. Create RemClaw/Debug.local.xcconfig to point telemetry, OAuth or the API at your own
// accounts WITHOUT editing this tracked file — which is how a secret ends up in a commit.
//
// Placed at the END deliberately: xcconfig resolves duplicate assignments last-one-wins, so
// an include at the top would be silently overridden by the settings above and the override
// would appear to do nothing.
//
// `#include?` is the optional form — a no-op when the file does not exist.
#include? "Debug.local.xcconfig"
